<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="003" project="code-quality-and-assurance-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Publish the governance baseline — six measures, confirmed not re-derived</title>
    <phase>1 The shared surface is knowable</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New documentation artifact built from mechanical measurement; no code, no tests, no hot-path edit.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Counting and tabulating against a closed set of six specified measures; the measurement recipes are mechanical.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P1-A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>docs,quality,baseline,measurement</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Publish projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r4/notes/baseline-2026-09.md recording FR-04's six measures. Five were already taken on 2026-09-03; this task CONFIRMS them against the current tree and records the measurement recipe for each so the nightly job (FR-12) and the equivalence check (FR-18) can measure their hit rates against a stable denominator.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Measure mechanically; report what you find, including where it disagrees with the spec.</role>
  <goal>A baseline document carrying all six FR-04 measures, each with the exact command used to produce it, and an explicit note on any measure that differs from spec.md's 2026-09-03 figure.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-04. The baseline exists so later mechanisms have a denominator: FR-18's equivalence-check hit rate accumulates against it, FR-12's usage-weight terciles are drawn from it, and FR-07 prioritises the criterion set by its ADR citation counts. Because the measurements were taken on 2026-09-03 and the branch has since merged 65 commits from master, this task confirms rather than assumes. A measure that has moved is a finding, not an error.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r4/notes/baseline-2026-09.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r4/spec.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="complete">Independent of 001 and 002 — measures the tree as it stands.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec">Scope (closed set of six): (a) &lt;extension&gt; yes/no ratio across 448 justifications; (b) &lt;existing&gt;none count (53 on 2026-09-03); (c) per-package import fan-in; (d) ADR citation counts across POML tasks; (e) &lt;escalation&gt;&lt;trigger&gt; firing count; (f) CLAUDE.md §6.5 amendment count. Do not add measures beyond these six.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">Scope (every measure): record the exact command that produced it. A number without a reproducible recipe cannot be re-measured by the nightly job and is worthless as a denominator.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope (repo-wide passes): MUST exclude .claude/worktrees/ and the ~17 sibling worktrees. A pass that walks siblings reports phantom counts.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope (no thresholds): this is observation only. MUST NOT derive or propose any threshold, target, or gate from these numbers.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope (honesty): where a confirmed measure differs from spec.md's 2026-09-03 figure, record BOTH and say which is current. Do not silently overwrite the spec's number.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Governance baseline measurement</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r4/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r4/plan.md</file>
      <file>CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the rigor-level declaration (STANDARD + reason). Read spec.md FR-04's six measures.</step>
    <step order="1">Measure (a) and (b) by scanning POML &lt;justification&gt; blocks across projects/*/tasks/ — excluding sibling worktrees.</step>
    <step order="2">Measure (c) per-package import fan-in across consuming surfaces for each of the 15 shared packages.</step>
    <step order="3">Measure (d) ADR citation counts across POML tasks; rank descending. This ordering is what FR-07 uses to prioritise within its criterion set.</step>
    <step order="4">Measure (e) &lt;escalation&gt;&lt;trigger&gt; occurrences and, where determinable, how many actually fired.</step>
    <step order="5">Measure (f) CLAUDE.md §6.5 amendment records across the repo.</step>
    <step order="6">Write the baseline document: one section per measure, each with value, command, and date. Flag any drift from the spec's 2026-09-03 figures.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set task 003 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document any deviation in projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r4/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a measure differs from spec.md's 2026-09-03 figure by more than ~10%, STOP and report before writing the baseline. A large drift over one day suggests the measurement recipe differs from the one originally used, not that the repository changed — and adopting a differently-derived number as the baseline would silently break FR-18's hit-rate comparison.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>No existing baseline artifact. Grep of projects/*/notes/ for baseline/measurement documents returns per-project scorecards (e.g. r3's SCORECARD.md) which measure code surfaces, not the governance surface.</existing>
    <extension>No. r3's scorecard grades code quality per surface on D1–D11; this records six governance-surface counts as a denominator for later mechanisms. Different subject, different consumer, different lifecycle.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>FR-18's equivalence-check hit rate has nothing to accumulate against, FR-12's usage terciles have no source, and FR-07 loses its stated prioritisation input — so the criterion set would be ordered by intuition.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r4/notes/baseline-2026-09.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the baseline document, all six FR-04 measures are present with a value.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given each measure, the exact reproducible command is recorded alongside it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the ADR citation counts, they are ranked descending so FR-07 can consume the ordering directly.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no threshold, target, or gate is proposed anywhere in the document.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no measurement command walks .claude/worktrees/ or sibling worktrees.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Any measure differing from spec.md's 2026-09-03 figure records both values and identifies which is current.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Maps spec.md FR-04 (closed set a–f). spec.md's 2026-09-03 reference figures: fan-in ui-components 54 surfaces, auth 37, communication-components 8, seven at 2, three at 1, two at 0; citations across 50 distinct ADRs led by ADR-021 (3,061), ADR-013 (2,131), ADR-038 (1,745), ADR-010 (1,527), ADR-028 (1,521), ADR-012 (1,210); &lt;existing&gt;none = 53 of 448.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
  <completion>
    <date>2026-09-04</date>
    <summary>All six FR-04 measures published in notes/baseline-2026-09.md, each with its reproducible command. Measure (c) briefly escalated and the escalation WITHDRAWN the same day: the stop rested on a claim that the recipe choice binds FR-12/FR-16/17/FR-18 downstream, which was false and unverified — grep of the spec, design and all 33 tasks shows nothing consumed measure (c) at all. Published using the consuming-deployables recipe; spec's 2026-09-03 figures marked unreproducible and superseded. The owner question that exposed this ("if used a lot, then what?") also reframed the objective as a PROCESS (planning-time assessment + CI revisit for drift), which surfaced a real gap and produced FR-19b / task 046.</summary>
    <files-modified>projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r4/notes/baseline-2026-09.md; projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r4/notes/task-003-escalation.md</files-modified>
    <findings>(1) ~32% of 459 &lt;extension&gt; answers lead with prose not a verdict — any mechanism parsing that field mis-buckets a third of it. (2) ADR citation ranks 4/5 swapped on a 6-of-1,520 gap; FR-07 consumes the ordering, so treat as tied. (3) Five of the six FR-04 measures still have NO named consumer — carry to wrap-up: point each at a mechanism or drop it.</findings>
  </completion>

</task>
